{
  "determination": "ABSENT",
  "cited_refs": ["CIP-009-6 R2 Part 2.1"],
  "rationale": "The governing text mandates that each recovery plan referenced in CIP-009-6 R1 be tested at least once every 15 calendar months via an actual incident, paper drill/tabletop exercise, or operational exercise, and the premise confirms testing itself is mandatory rather than elective. The candidate only addresses existence of a documented recovery plan and review for accuracy upon infrastructure changes, containing no periodic testing obligation, no 15-calendar-month interval, and none of the three permitted test methods, so it does not satisfy CIP-009-6 R2 Part 2.1."
}

DETERMINATION COMPLETE

